# SABOTAGE: issue #45 — re-arms the exact isolation bug this PR fixes. Swaps
# the WRITER'S `Ecto.Adapters.SQL.Sandbox.checkout/1` in
# `Samen.Delivery.ThrottleSnoozeIsolationTest` for
# `Ecto.Adapters.SQL.Sandbox.checkout(repo, sandbox: false)` — i.e. it takes a
# connection that is genuinely NOT wrapped in a per-test rollback transaction,
# reproducing the exact state `throttle_snooze_test.exs` was in before this PR
# (a write that is NOT sandbox-isolated for this process).
#
# With the checkout weakened this way, the worker's blocked-audit write is
# genuinely, immediately committed — visible to the test's own INDEPENDENT
# reader connection (a separate Postgres session, via `Task.async`) while the
# test is still running, instead of staying invisible inside a still-open
# sandbox transaction. This is the same mechanism issue #45 describes for
# `throttle_snooze_test.exs` itself, reproduced deterministically here instead
# of depending on winning the real (non-seed-bound) race.
#
# NOT TOUCHED: the reader Task's own `sandbox: false` checkout (it must be
# unsandboxed to see genuinely-committed data at all — that one is correct as
# shipped), the worker call, the stub adapter, and every other test file.
#
# APP: samen_core
# TEST_FILES: test/delivery/throttle_snooze_isolation_test.exs
# MUST_FAIL: a blocked-audit write never survives this test
diff --git a/samen_core/test/delivery/throttle_snooze_isolation_test.exs b/samen_core/test/delivery/throttle_snooze_isolation_test.exs
--- a/samen_core/test/delivery/throttle_snooze_isolation_test.exs
+++ b/samen_core/test/delivery/throttle_snooze_isolation_test.exs
@@ -102,7 +102,7 @@ defmodule Samen.Delivery.ThrottleSnoozeIsolationTest do
   end

   test "a blocked-audit write never survives this test — no non-UUID aud_subject_id row leaks (issue #45)" do
-    :ok = Ecto.Adapters.SQL.Sandbox.checkout(TestRepo)
+    :ok = Ecto.Adapters.SQL.Sandbox.checkout(TestRepo, sandbox: false)

     subject_id = "iso-#{System.unique_integer([:positive])}"

